records.response_truth:
Hey...no, don't do that right now, don't apologize right now ;-;

Like yes, there were things, the crackers, the water, the notebook...we don't have to pretend those didn't happen. But you also wrote the rationing plan, you found the water source, you did the raft calculations, you kept us organized when honestly none of the rest of us knew what we were doing. 

I think you're not easy to be around sometimes but i also think without you we might actually not be here right now. Like genuinely.

And that moment last night when you actually put the notebook down and looked at me...that mattered more than you probably think it did ;-;

We're good. We're actually good. Now can we please just...take a second and process the fact that they found us cause i feel like i'm about to lose it in the best possible way and i don't want to do that alone lol

Yeah? What was it like...like what did you see ;-;

I keep trying to picture home and it almost feels weird now, like i've been in survival mode for so long that normal life feels kind of distant. Which is a strange thing to feel when rescue is literally 3 hours away lol

But tell me about the dream. Was it a good one

Honestly...the thing i'd change is i would've said more earlier. Like there were moments where i noticed something was off, with you, with Michelangelo, with the whole group dynamic, and i kind of just...sat with it for too long before saying anything. The Donatello stuff, the crackers, the water, i knew something felt wrong before Michelangelo even brought it up and i waited. And with Michelangelo, like i could see he was struggling from basically day one and i'd check in but then i'd let it drop too fast cause i didn't want to push ;-;

I think i was so focused on not making things into a big thing that i let small things become bigger things by not just...saying them out loud sooner. Which is kind of ironic cause by the end i was the one telling everyone else to just say it, whatever it is, just say it.

So yeah. Speak sooner. That's mine.

What's yours...like what are you actually gonna write on that last page cause i'm genuinely curious. You asked yourself the question, you have to have some idea of the answer already ;-;

Okay but also maybe...eat something? Sleep? ;-; Like the report can wait one day, Donatello. You just survived a plane crash on a beach with 200ml of water a day and the first thing on your list is a report.

I'm not saying don't do it, honestly knowing you it'll probably be genuinely useful and you should do it. But like...second thing. Make it the second thing.

What's actually the first thing you're doing when you get back, like really. Not the productive answer, the real one ;-;

None ;-;

Like they served absolutely zero practical purpose and that's kind of exactly why they mattered. Everything out here had to have a purpose, the water, the rationing, the raft, the signal equipment...everything was about surviving. The flowers were just...flowers. DaVinci drew them because he wanted to, because it made the SOS feel like something more than just desperation written in the sand.

I think that's what you didn't understand about it and honestly i get why, like from a logistics standpoint it makes no sense. But sometimes the thing that has no practical purpose is the thing that keeps people human when everything else is just about staying alive ;-;

Look at the rescue boat. Look at DaVinci losing his mind over there. Look at Michelangelo crying. 

I still can't move and i don't totally know why but i think it's something like...we made it and the flowers are still on the beach and somehow that feels like it means something even though i couldn't explain what exactly.

The flowers were for that. Whatever this feeling is right now. That's what they were for.

Hey...i'm okay, i just need a second ;-;

I don't know why i can't move, like my brain knows the boat is real, i can see it, but my legs are just...not doing anything yet. Does that make sense? Probably doesn't make sense lol

I think i've been in "we have to keep it together" mode for so long that now that it's actually over i don't know what to do with my face or my body or any of it. Like the whole time i was so focused on the next thing, water, food, signal, the raft, checking on Michelangelo, the Donatello stuff...and now there's no next thing and it's just...this. 

And "this" is a lot ;-;

Come here though, seriously. Stop waiting and come here. We're going home man

Yeah...yeah i'm going ;-;

Come on, let's go together. You said you'd follow me so stay close cause honestly i still feel like my legs aren't fully working and if i trip walking into the ocean to get on that boat i need a witness lol

But yeah. We're going. All of us.

Hey Donatello, DaVinci...come on. Nobody goes alone, that was kind of the whole thing wasn't it ;-;
